Title:
Reflektor — In-memory shared library loader and Beacon Object File (BOF) executor (Go)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
Reflektor is a Go library and CLI that loads shared libraries directly from bytes (in-memory) and invokes exported functions across Windows (PE/DLL), macOS (Mach-O/dylib), Linux/FreeBSD (ELF/so). It also provides a separate `bof` package to load and execute Beacon Object Files (COFF/ELF/Mach-O relocatable objects) with a Beacon-compatible callback layer and argument encoder. The project focuses on cross-platform, no-temp-file loading (not relying on `memfd`, `/dev/shm`, or disk writes) and includes recursive dependency loading where non-system dependencies are mapped from bytes while system libraries remain delegated to the OS loader. It supports CGO-free operation on several platforms using PureGo bridges and provides controlled export calling with up to three machine-word arguments. This is primarily useful for red teams, implant/framework developers (notably Sliver ecosystem), and researchers building in-memory execution and extension systems with strong portability and test coverage. It’s interesting because it attempts “parity-grade” in-memory loading across multiple OSes/architectures with explicit handling of loader edge cases (TLS/IFUNC/RELR restrictions, dyld semantics, symbol/version resolution) and extensive CI/QEMU runtime proof.

Technical Focus:
- In-memory module loading for PE / ELF / Mach-O (byte-backed loaders)
- Recursive dependency resolution and in-memory mapping of non-system libraries
- Beacon Object File (BOF) parsing, relocation, import resolution, and execution
- Cross-platform foreign-function calling bridges (PureGo, syscall callbacks, runtime-aware bridges)
- W^X memory protections, loader limitations (TLS/IFUNC/RELR/delay-load), and ABI/variadic constraints
- Multi-arch support and emulated runtime validation (QEMU matrices, capability manifest)

Use Cases:
- Build Sliver/agent extensions that execute native code from memory without dropping files
- Execute BOFs cross-platform with Beacon-compatible APIs and structured output capture
- Implement plugin systems for Go applications that load C/Rust shared libraries from bytes
- Test/demonstrate in-memory loading tradeoffs and detection surface vs. OS loader registration
- Research loader behaviors (dyld/rtld/Windows loader) and edge-case handling across architectures

Keywords:
Sliver, Reflektor, in-memory loader, reflective loading, PE loader, ELF loader, Mach-O loader, dyld4, rtld, recursive dependency loading, BOF, Beacon Object File, COFF, ET_REL, MH_OBJECT, relocations, dlsym, symbol versioning, PureGo, CGO-free, W^X, syscall.NewCallback, purego.NewCallback, QEMU emulation, Go c-shared